Proposed for world (owner of street_walker_cards.gd tonight), measured in a throwaway worktree (prof3.patch arms):
StreetWalkerCards.place(): (1) the walk grid's fill cached per texture (today WALK_FILL.get's default
StreetCopWalk.fill_of(path) builds two strings every tick, eagerly, even when the key hits); (2) one
global_transform set instead of global_rotation + global_scale + global_position (each setter re-reads the
parent's global transform). Same values up to float rounding of the intermediate decomposition (skew 0).
(3) row_of(): read the street_row meta when present before formatting RigHeadCard.key_of's "%s/%s".

static var _fills: Dictionary = {}

static func _fill(tex: Texture2D) -> float:
	if _fills.has(tex):
		return _fills[tex]
	var f: float = WALK_FILL.get(tex.resource_path.get_file(), StreetCopWalk.fill_of(tex.resource_path))
	_fills[tex] = f
	return f

